oceed rather than abort\"`","tests/scripts/test_mutation_sandbox.py:684 test_falsey_ci_values_do_not_waive_the_sandbox and :872 test_the_ci_fail_open_warning_names_the_variable_and_its_value both drive the CI env={\"CI\": ...} branch"],"finding":"The plan removes the CI-keyed branch in wrap() (scripts/mutation_sandbox.py) but its patch-site inventory omits the existing tests in tests/scripts/test_mutation_sandbox.py that pin the behavior being deleted. Three tests assert the CI fall-back proceeds unsandboxed and warns: test_ci_runner_proceeds_unsandboxed_with_a_warning (line 666), test_falsey_ci_values_do_not_waive_the_sandbox (line 682), and test_the_ci_fail_open_warning_names_the_variable_and_its_value (line 862). All three will fail once the branch is gone, yet the ACs only add new tests and never list these as patch-sites to delete/rewrite.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fce29202cf4b90369","impact":0.85,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria (all four items) — enumerating wrap(), _mutation.yml, and lanes but no existing-test patch-sites","norm_id":"n71c3f412ab03251f","priority":0.7556,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["tests/scripts/test_mutation_sandbox.py::test_ci_runner_proceeds_unsandboxed_with_a_warning — after branch removal wrap({\"CI\":\"true\"}) raises SandboxUnavailable, so this test's `argv == [\"/bin/true\"]` assertion fails; not listed for update.","tests/scripts/test_mutation_sandbox.py::test_the_ci_fail_open_warning_names_the_variable_and_its_value — asserts the CI warning is emitted; the warning no longer fires, test fails; not listed for update.","tests/scripts/test_mutation_sandbox.py::test_falsey_ci_values_do_not_waive_the_sandbox — now redundant/misleading once CI never waives; not listed for update."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"In the ACs or a Scope note, list tests/scripts/test_mutation_sandbox.py and specify: delete/rewrite the three CI-fall-back tests so they assert SandboxUnavailable is raised (or the opt-out path), replacing the current assertions that the run proceeds unsandboxed.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8889,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Encode the ordering constraint in the ACs: the `_mutation.yml` opt-out (AC3) must land in the same change as, or before, the branch removal (AC1), so the lane never runs without a mechanism or a declared waiver.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5e"],"criteria":["E6","T4"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.164,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'That lane must therefore declare the waiver explicitly before the branch is removed, or it will start aborting.'","AC1 and AC3 are listed as independent checkboxes with no stated ordering dependency between them."],"finding":"The plan states in prose that the _mutation.yml lane 'must declare the waiver explicitly before the branch is removed, or it will start aborting,' but the acceptance criteria (AC1 removes the branch, AC3 sets the opt-out) do not encode this ordering as a sequencing constraint, so an executor could remove the branch first and break the lane.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f6bdfb09c3e9ae915","impact":0.536,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria AC1/AC3; 'The lane that relies on the CI branch today' section","norm_id":"nd0a76b87c6e3cb3e","priority":0.536,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An executor implements AC1 (remove branch) and lands it before AC3 (set opt-out in _mutation.yml), causing the mutation gate to abort in CI."],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"Add to AC3 (or a sequencing note): 'This waiver must be committed atomically with, or prior to, the branch removal in AC1.'","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"medium","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["vague/subjective terms present: better"],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_prima